---
<div class="sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="head"><span class="eyebrow rv">Who does what</span><h2 class="split">Agents do the building. Engineers do the understanding.</h2></div>
<div class="wwd">
<div class="card rv"><span class="tag">AI agents</span><h3>Build everything needed</h3><ul class="ul"><li>Turn briefs into user stories and architecture drafts</li><li>Write code, tests and documentation</li><li>Run test, security and accessibility checks on every change</li><li>Deploy in stages and monitor around the clock</li></ul></div>
<div class="card ind rv" style="--d:100ms"><span class="tag">Engineers</span><h3>Understand and make it better</h3><ul class="ul"><li>Learn your business, users and constraints</li><li>Make the architecture and trade-off calls</li><li>Review every change before it ships</li><li>Turn what the agents learn into a better next version</li></ul></div>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:64px"></div>
<div class="pbk">
<div class="pbr rv"><span class="n">01</span><h3>Before we start</h3><p>A one-to-two-week discovery. You get a written summary of goals, users, risks, architecture and a costed plan. If we think you shouldn't build it, we'll say so.</p></div>
<div class="pbr rv"><span class="n">02</span><h3>Every two weeks</h3><p>A demo of working software and a written update in four parts: done, next, risks, and decisions we need from you.</p></div>
<div class="pbr rv"><span class="n">03</span><h3>How we talk</h3><p>A shared channel with your team, replies the same working day, and one named delivery lead accountable for the project.</p></div>
<div class="pbr rv"><span class="n">04</span><h3>Our quality bar</h3><p>Agents write tests for every change. Every release passes automated tests, a security scan and accessibility checks, and an engineer reviews it before it ships.</p></div>
<div class="pbr rv"><span class="n">05</span><h3>Handover</h3><p>Documentation, runbooks, architecture notes and a recorded walkthrough. Your team should be able to run the system without us.</p></div>
<div class="pbr rv"><span class="n">06</span><h3>Your code, your access</h3><p>Code lives in your repositories from day one. When we finish, we remove our access and confirm it in writing.</p></div>
</div>
</div></div>
